theorem rational-below-a-positive-rational
  note        Half of a positive rational is a positive rational below it.
  let x ∈ ℚ                                                           (H1)
  assume x > 0                                                        (H2)
  then there exists y ∈ ℚ such that y > 0 and y < x

1.  x/2 > 0
    inequalities, from H2

2.  x/2 < x
    inequalities, from H2

3.  There exists y ∈ ℚ such that y > 0 and y < x.
    exhibit, from 1, 2
